From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robgallardof <robgallardof@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:03:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Run on Windows and Linux: cross-platform paths, no venv
 segfault, pin mcp<2

The server hard-coded macOS paths, so on Windows and Linux it could not import
DaVinciResolveScript and the LUT tools never found a LUT.

- New resolve_mcp/paths.py: scripting API dir, Modules dir, fusionscript library
  and LUT folders for macOS, Windows and Linux, following Blackmagic's scripting
  README. RESOLVE_SCRIPT_API and RESOLVE_SCRIPT_LIB still override.
- connection.py: sets the variables Blackmagic expects before import, and on
  Windows sets PYTHONHOME to the base interpreter inside a virtualenv.
  fusionscript.dll otherwise crashes the whole process (segfault).
- Accurate connection messages: "not running" was printed even with Resolve
  open (Free edition / external scripting disabled).
- color.apply_lut and dailies search every LUT folder of the current OS;
  _find_lut tolerates roots that don't exist.
- pyproject: mcp<2. mcp 2.x renamed FastMCP and the server no longer imports.
- tests/test_paths.py: 4 tests (macOS unchanged, Windows, Linux, env overrides).

Verified on Windows 11 + Resolve 21.0.4: before, "module not found at
/Library/..."; after, the module imports and the connection is reported correctly.
